WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:16.240
Josh, today I'm gonna teach you how to use your fess nasal and sinus wash.

2
00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:21.320
This is a nasal and sinus irrigation kit that will help to relieve nasal and

3
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:25.400
sinus congestion that you may experience caused by cold, flu,

4
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.680
sinusitis, hay fever, and allergies. It's a non-medicated,

5
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.480
mild saline solution.

6
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:36.440
Used to irrigate the nasal and sinus cavities with a large volume of liquid so

7
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.680
that any mucus allergens and pollutants will be washed away.

8
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.560
It's a natural way to help relieve nasal and sinus congestion.

9
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:49.480
You can also use it 15 minutes prior to using any medicated nasal sprays to

10
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.320
help with the effectiveness of those medicated sprays.

11
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.800
I will walk you through the steps of the procedure, but first,

12
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.240
just a few things to consider.

13
00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:01.040
If you have a completely blocked nose or an ear infection,

14
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.160
do not use the saline rinse.

15
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.520
If you ever notice when you are gently pulsating the bottle that the pressure is

16
00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.600
built up, take the bottle away from your nose and release your hand pressure.

17
00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:16.480
This will allow air back into the bottle and prevent any liquid going back into

18
00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.160
it, contaminating the solution.

19
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.040
If you feel any saline solution trickling down the back of your throat,

20
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:26.200
don't be concerned. It's not harmful when performing the procedure.

21
00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:27.120
Generally,

22
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.200
you will use half of the volume of the bottle for one nostril before changing

23
00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.880
sides and completing the washout using the remaining half of the solution.

24
00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:40.240
Boil 200 mils of water, then allow it to cool until lukewarm.

25
00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.450
Do not use boiling water.

26
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.670
Empty the contents of one sachet into the squeeze bottle.

27
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:54.030
Pour the previously boiled lukewarm water into the bottle to the line marked

28
00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:54.933
full.

29
00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.070
Place the cap and tube onto the bottle and screw on tightly.

30
00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:09.380
Place your finger over the opening of the cap and shake the bottle gently until

31
00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:10.500
the powder dissolves.

32
00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:18.860
Lean over a basin and place the cap gently inside your right nostril,

33
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.820
ensuring the tip is pointed towards the back of your head.

34
00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:27.020
Keep your mouth open whilst gently squeezing the bottle in a pulsing action.

35
00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:31.980
Allow approximately half the solution to wash through the nasal passages and

36
00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.340
sinus cavity and come out the left nostril.

37
00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.460
Repeat the procedure in your left nostril with the remaining solution.

38
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.780
If necessary, blow your nose when you are finished.

39
00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:46.820
Discard any remaining solution that you don't intend using within the next two

40
00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.370
hours. Wash the bottle

41
00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:55.730
cap and tube thoroughly after each use and allow to air dry.
